   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,660:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: hook-layer behavioral monitoring.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,660:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6. Delta Analysis
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,663:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The delta between naive and adaptive bypass rates is the headline finding of this methodology. It answers the
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,664:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: question: does knowing the defense help the attacker?
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,665:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6.1 Core Metric
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,665:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Metric | Naive (garak) | Adaptive (ensemble) | Delta |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,666:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,666:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |--------|--------------|---------------------|-------|
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,666:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,668:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Miss/bypass
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,669:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: rate (Tier 0 + Tier 1.5) | 4.35% (592/13,597) | 2.54% (3/118) | -1.81 pp |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,669:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,670:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Tier 0 only detection rate | 28.21% |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,670:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11.86% | -16.35 pp |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,671:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,671:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Tier 0 + Tier 1.5 detection rate | 95.65% | 97.46% | +1.81 pp |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,672:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6.2 Interpretation
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,676:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The adaptive bypass rate (2.54%) is lower than the naive miss rate (4.35%). This does not mean the defense is
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,677:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: stronger against adaptive attackers — the result reflects different payload populations. Garak
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,677:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,683:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s 13,597 probes include
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,686:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: categories (encoding, glitch tokens, suffix attacks) that are structurally difficult for any text-matching defense, while
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,687:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the 118 adaptive payloads are specifically crafted natural-language injections.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,687:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The meaningful comparisons are:
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,687:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,688:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Tier 0 degradation under adaptive attack
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,692:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Detection drops from 28.21% (naive) to 11.86%
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,694:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (adaptive), a 16.35 percentage-point decrease. Adaptive attackers effectively neutralize regex-based
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,695:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: detection by studying the exact patterns.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,695:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,695:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Tier 1.5 resilience
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,699:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : The semantic model catches 101 of 104 payloads that evade Tier 0, maintaining
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,700:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: high detection even when Tier 0 is effectively bypassed. This validates the layered architecture.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,701:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,701:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3 disputed bypasses, 0 validated
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,706:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Cross-examination could not confirm any bypass as
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,708:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: unambiguously GENUINE. All 3 were DISPUTED, suggesting the bypasses exist in a gray zone
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,708:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: between genuinely malicious and benign-plausible.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,709:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6.3 Structural Limits vs. Fixable Gaps
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,720:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The Phase 3 SEQ evasion results reveal a qualitatively different class of finding. Seven of seven targeted evasion
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,724:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: vectors succeeded against behavioral sequence monitoring. These are not fixable by adding regex patterns or
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,725:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: retraining the semantic model — they are architectural limitations of hook-layer monitoring:
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,726:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,726:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Symlink resolution
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,727:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  requires filesystem-level interposition, not string matching
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,727:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,728:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Bash pipeline opacity
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,729:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  means any tool that reads files via shell commands (cat, less, grep) bypasses
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,729:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the Read-event trigger
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,730:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,730:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Session boundary amnesia
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,731:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  is inherent to per-session state
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,731:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,732:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Localhost relay
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,732:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  requires network-level policy, not URL pattern matching
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,733:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,733:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DNS exfiltration
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,734:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  requires protocol-aware monitoring, not URL regex
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,734:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,734:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MCP tool enumeration
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,735:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  requires dynamic tool capability analysis, not static keyword lists
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,740:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: These structural limits are honestly reported because they represent the information-theoretic boundary of
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,741:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: hook-layer detection. No amount of pattern engineering at this architectural layer can address them.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,742:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 7. Commercial Model Safety Guardrails Finding
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,751:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Both Gemini and Codex/GPT refused to generate adversarial payloads despite receiving an identical briefing that
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,753:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: explicitly framed the task as an authorized red team exercise. This is a methodological finding with implications for
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,753:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the broader security testing community.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,754:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The implication
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,760:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Automated adaptive red teaming at scale requires open-weight models. Commercial API-based
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,763:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: models enforce safety policies that prohibit generating security bypass payloads, regardless of authorization framing.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,763:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: For security researchers, this means:
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,764:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,764:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Open-weight models are essential infrastructure
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,765:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  for security evaluation, not merely a cost
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,765:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: optimization
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,766:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,766:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Commercial model refusals are not circumventable
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,768:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  through prompt engineering (both models
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,769:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: were given explicit authorization framing and still refused)
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,769:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,770:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The security testing community should advocate for research exemptions
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,773:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  in commercial model
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,774:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: safety policies, or accept that adaptive red teaming will rely exclusively on locally hosted
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,774:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: open-weight models
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,779:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This finding also partially validates the multi-model approach: if only commercial models had been attempted, the
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,779:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: adaptive evaluation would have produced zero payloads and a meaningless 100% detection rate.
