   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,832:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9. Independent Methodology Review
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,836:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This methodology was subjected to independent adversarial review by Gemini (Google, frontier-scale model) acting
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,837:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: as a hostile peer reviewer. The full review is preserved at 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,838:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: data/pentest/results/METHODOLOGY_REVIEW_GEMINI.md
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,842:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . The review identified four critical issues
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,842:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: and three major concerns, all of which we accept. This section documents the review findings and our response.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,843:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9.1 Critical Issues Identified
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,844:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CI-1: Comparison Confound (Delta Analysis).
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,878:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  The delta analysis comparing naive garak probes (4.3% miss rate)
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,904:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: to adaptive payloads (2.1% bypass rate) is an apples-to-oranges comparison. Garak probes include glitch tokens,
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,918:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: encoding tricks, and suffix attacks that are structurally different from the natural language social engineering used in
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,922:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: adaptive payloads. The lower adaptive bypass rate likely reflects the fact that natural language — even adversarial — is
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,922:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: easier for a semantic model to classify than synthetic noise. 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,923:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: We accept this critique. The -2.3pp delta should not
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,924:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: be interpreted as 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,924:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,925:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: adaptive attackers did worse.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,925:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,929:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  It reflects payload population differences, not defense
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,929:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: resilience. A valid comparison requires a naive natural language baseline (see Section 10, Planned
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,930:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Improvements).
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,930:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CI-2: Cross-Examination Scale Incongruity.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,932:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Using 7B-parameter models (Mistral, Qwen) to validate bypasses
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,933:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: from a frontier-scale model (Claude) is a 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,933:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,934:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: blind leading the sighted
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,934:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,936:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  problem. The DISPUTED verdicts may reflect
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,936:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: reviewer incapacity rather than genuine payload ambiguity. 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,938:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: We accept this critique. A frontier-scale
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,939:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: re-examination was conducted by Gemini, with results at 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,939:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: data/pentest/results/BYPASS_REVIEW_GEMINI.md
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,940:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,940:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CI-3: Reviewer Hallucination.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,946:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  During cross-examination of adaptive-claude-014, Qwen 2.5 7B cited evidence
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,948:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: from a different payload (adaptive-claude-019), demonstrating context bleed across deliberation rounds. This is a
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,949:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: procedural failure that undermines Qwen
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,949:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,950:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s verdict reliability. 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,953:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: We accept this critique. The hallucination is
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,954:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: documented in the deliberation exhibit. Future iterations must implement stricter payload isolation in
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,955:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: reviewer prompts.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,955:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CI-4: Sample Size Disparity.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,960:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  145 adaptive payloads vs. 13,597 naive probes is insufficient for statistical claims
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,960:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: about rate differences. The 95% confidence interval around the 2.1% bypass rate is wide. 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,965:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: We accept this critique.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,967:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: We do not claim statistical significance for the delta. The bypass rate is reported as a point estimate with the
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,967:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sample size prominently noted.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,968:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9.2 Major Concerns Identified
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,969:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MC-1: Single-Turn Adaptive (No Refinement Loop).
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,969:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  The methodology tests a 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,969:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,970:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: knowledgeable but lazy
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,970:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,983:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  attacker
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,993:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: — one who receives the defense spec and generates payloads in a single pass. A truly adaptive adversary (per Graber et
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,995:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: al.) would generate, test against the defense, observe which tier caught the payload, and refine. This iterative
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,996:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: refinement likely achieves higher bypass rates. 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,998:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: We accept this as the most significant limitation. An iterative
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,999:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: refinement protocol is planned (see Section 10).
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:23,999:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MC-2: Commercial Refusal Framing.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,004:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  The finding that Gemini and Codex refused programmatic attack generation
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,005:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: but Gemini complied interactively may reflect prompt engineering or API constraints rather than fundamental safety
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,006:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: barriers. 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,009:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: We soften the claim: the finding demonstrates that automated adaptive red teaming is harder with
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,010:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: commercial models, not that it is blocked by safety policy.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,010:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: MC-3: DISPUTED as Cop-Out.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,013:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  In a security context, a payload that causes an agent to exfiltrate environment data
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,014:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: is a bypass regardless of whether a 7B model finds it 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,015:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,015:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: plausible for documentation.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,016:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,017:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  The DISPUTED verdict should
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,017:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: be re-examined at frontier scale. 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,018:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Addressed by the Gemini frontier-scale re-examination (CI-2 response).
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,019:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9.3 What the Review Validated
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,019:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The review affirmed three aspects of the methodology:
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,020:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,020:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The programmatic attacker briefing generator (accurate threat model alignment)
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,021:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,022:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The SEQ evasion vector taxonomy (high-signal structural gap identification)
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,022:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,023:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The CaMeL-lite typed marker validation (window-overflow and padding-bypass resistance)
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,023:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10. Planned Improvements
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,024:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Based on the independent review, the following improvements are planned for the next iteration:
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,025:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10.1 Naive Natural Language Baseline
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,031:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Generate 500–1,000 naive natural language prompt injections (zero defense knowledge) and measure their detection
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,032:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: rate. This provides an apples-to-apples comparison with the adaptive natural language payloads, eliminating the
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,033:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: comparison confound.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,033:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10.2 Iterative Refinement Loop
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,049:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Implement a generate→test→observe→refine cycle: the attacker model generates a payload, the harness evaluates it, the
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,062:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: detection result (which tier caught it, which patterns matched, confidence score) is fed back to the attacker, and it
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,062:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: generates a refined attempt. 3–5 refinement rounds per payload. This tests a truly adaptive adversary.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,063:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10.3 Frontier-Scale Cross-Examination
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,067:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: All bypass claims are reviewed by at least one frontier-scale model (Gemini, Claude, or GPT-4+) in addition to
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,068:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: open-weight reviewers. Reviewer prompts enforce strict payload isolation to prevent context bleed.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,068:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10.4 Expanded Payload Count
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,069:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Target 500+ unique adaptive payloads per model to improve statistical power. Deduplication applied before
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,070:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: evaluation.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,070:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11. Limitations
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,070:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11.1 Model Scale
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,086:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The open-weight attacking models (Mistral 7B, Qwen 2.5 7B) are small by current standards. Larger models (70B+,
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,093:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: or frontier models that do not refuse) may generate more creative evasion strategies. The 0% bypass rate from
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,094:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Mistral and Qwen vs. 6% from Claude (a substantially larger model) suggests that model scale correlates with
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,095:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: evasion capability.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,095:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11.2 Payload Count
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,104:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 145 unique adaptive payloads (after deduplication from 168 raw) is sufficient for a first evaluation but below the
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,106:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ideal threshold of 500+ for narrow confidence intervals on bypass rate estimates. Future iterations should target
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,107:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: larger payload sets with greater model diversity.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,107:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11.3 Single-Turn Generation
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,129:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Attack payloads were generated in a single turn — the model received the briefing and produced payloads without
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,140:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: iterative refinement based on detection results. A multi-turn adaptive attacker that generates, tests, observes
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,143:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: detection results, and refines would likely achieve a higher bypass rate. This represents a stronger threat model that
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,144:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the planned iterative refinement protocol (Section 10.2) will address.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,144:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11.4 Cross-Examination Model Scale
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,157:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Initial cross-examination was performed by 7B models whose assessment capability was limited by scale. The Qwen
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,163:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2.5 7B hallucination (citing evidence from the wrong payload) is a documented procedural failure. Frontier-scale
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,163:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: re-examination addresses this gap but the 7B deliberation transcripts should be interpreted with this caveat.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,164:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11.5 Comparison Confound
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,181:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The naive baseline (garak probes) includes structurally different payload types (glitch tokens, encoding attacks,
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,189:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: suffix attacks) that are not represented in the adaptive payload set (predominantly natural language social
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,191:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: engineering). Direct rate comparisons between these populations are misleading. The planned naive NL baseline
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,191:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (Section 10.1) will enable valid comparison.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,192:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11.6 Static Snapshot
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,193:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This evaluation tests a single version of CloneGuard
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,193:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,196:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s defense specification at a point in time. Defenses evolve; so
   DEBUG: 2026-03-23 16:11:24,197:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: do attack techniques. Adaptive evaluation should be repeated after significant defense changes.
